# s29c_harness.oot — 2.9 wave-3 H-later + H-same println SECRET harness pointer
# Date: 2026-08-12
# Scope: SPRINT 2.9 wave-3 smoke rails only (no Domain Expert product land)

## Harness

| Item | Path |
|------|------|
| Smoke | `ooda/scripts/s29_println_guard_smoke.sh` |
| Binary | `OODAC_BIN` or `ooda/oodac/oodac` |
| Fixtures | ephemeral under `$TMPDIR/s29_println_guard_$$` (not repo root) |
| Product | `ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret.oo` (`check_secret_println_sinks`) + `c_emit_print.oo` (`c_emit_println`) — do not rewrite |
| Wave-1 pointer | `audit/s29_harness.oot` (bare IDENT + string no-FP + eprintln) |
| Wave-2 pointer | `audit/s29b_harness.oot` (`println((1), tok)` grouped later-arg) |

One smoke. No second 2.9 script.

## Rails (wave-3 keeps wave-1 + wave-2)

| Kind | Case |
|------|------|
| FAIL-closed | `// SECRET: tok` then `println(tok)` (bare IDENT) |
| PASS no-FP | `println("tok")` string literal when `tok` is SECRET name (no `ERR secret`) |
| FAIL-closed | `// SECRET: tok` then `eprintln(tok)` **if product** names `eprintln` |
| FAIL-closed (H-later) | `// SECRET: tok` then `println((1), tok)` — grouped first arg, SECRET later IDENT |
| FAIL-closed (H-same) | `// SECRET: tok` then `println(("x") + tok)` — grouping then `+` SECRET in the **same** arg |
| PASS no-FP | `println((1), 2)` public grouping while unused SECRET name `tok` exists |

Both H-later and H-same are dual-path: `check` **and** `emit-c` must print `ERR	secret` (rc≠0). Exit 0 only if all rails hold. Missing `ERR	secret` on either path is FAIL.

Wave-3 **exact** H-same shape is `println(("x") + tok)`. Extra wrap `println((("x") + tok))` is **not** this rail (`ERR	type` is not a SECRET seal).

## Run

```
cd /home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda
OODAC_BIN=./oodac/oodac bash scripts/s29_println_guard_smoke.sh
```

Prefer a cwd without a stale `.ooda-cache` (check-cache can false-OK).

## Live prove (this host, 2026-08-12T19:43Z)

Clean cwd `/tmp/s29c_harness_prove_*`, `OODAC_BIN=ooda/oodac/oodac` (ELF **07:49** / **04:49 -1000**; 962960 B; md5 `a44ee35eb344837009697e2c9d4e4662`; BuildID `a93cfd09506ba87497379f66b6c7047dee02573d`). Smoke **194** L; md5 `2ad0ee9592709771015e8fc55298a81e`. `bash -n` PASS.

| Rail | emit-c | check |
|------|--------|-------|
| `println(tok)` | `ERR	secret` | `ERR	secret` |
| `println("tok")` | no `ERR secret` | no `ERR secret` |
| `eprintln(tok)` | `ERR	secret` | `ERR	secret` |
| `println((1), tok)` | `ERR	secret` (`oo_print_int((1LL));` then refuse; `tok` not printed) | **FN** `OK` rc=0 |
| `println(("x") + tok)` | **FN leak** rc=0 `oo_print_str(oo_str_concat((oo_str_lit("x")), tok))` | **FN** `OK` rc=0 |
| `println((1), 2)` | no `ERR secret` | no `ERR secret` |

Smoke **exit 1** is the fail-closed signal. Wave-3 rails are **not** green on this ELF. WT source has paren `depth` (`c_emit_secret.oo` L191; `c_emit_print.oo` L19 `d`) but the shipping host was not rebuilt. Do not treat exit 1 as a harness bug.

## Residual (documented, not a fail)

- **Full IFC / `#[Secret]` / interp `${}`:** path-A ident scan only; not DESIGN taint.
- **2.9 unify:** stmt `println` may still refuse via token IDENT + `check_secret_println_sinks` rather than `c_secret_emit_guard`. This harness proves refuse/no-FP on the two named shapes, not the helper.
- **Other grouping shapes:** nested `f(g(), tok)`, method `RPAREN` then `+`, extra wrap `((("x") + tok))`, eprintln H-same / H-later are not this rail.
- **LLVM / wasm / emit-bc:** not dual-path in this smoke.

end of s29c_harness.oot
